  "protocol": {
    "summary": "Standing barefoot, knees straight, chin to chest then bend forward sliding hands down the legs to the floor, hold 1 s, return; metronome-paced 8 s (slow) or 3 s (fast) per phase; series repeated lifting a 10-kg barbell (hand position standardised). iEMG (0.1 s) of right ES at L3; Chattanooga lumbar motion monitor (T12 to S1).",
    "how_to_simulate": [
      "Scale to the cohort (10 F / 12 M, 21 y, ~168 cm, ~64 kg)",
      "Sweep trunk flexion quasi-statically from upright to full flexion with knees straight (slow series), no load or 10 kg in both hands with arms hanging",
      "Record lumbar (T12-S1) flexion when the erector spinae under the L3 electrode falls silent (onset) and, extending, when it returns (cessation)",
      "Report each as % of the model's maximum lumbar flexion (Sarti: 55.7±8.0 deg no load, 56.8±6.7 deg with 10 kg, slow)"
    ],
    "subject_model": {
      "sex": "10 F / 12 M",
      "age": 21.45,
      "height_cm": 168.2,
      "weight_kg": 64.1,
      "disc_area_mm2": null,
      "source": "Sarti 2001 Table 1 (n-weighted means of F and M)"
    },
    "notes": "Values as printed in Table 2 ('% ± SD'); some SDs are implausibly small (e.g. CP ±1) but are copied unchanged. Speed significantly delayed MS (F vs S, P<0.01); load had no significant effect. Relative lumbar motion time (Table 4) and raw iEMG (uV) not extracted."
  },
